<title>SINGAPORE: Best bid in Sri Lanka naphtha tender, minus $1.18.</title>
<headline>Best bid in Sri Lanka naphtha tender, minus $1.18.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The highest bid in Sri Lankan state-owned Ceylon Petroleum Corp's (CPC) tender to sell naphtha was at a discount of $1.18 a barrel to Singapore spot quotes, on a free-on-board basis from Colombo, a CPC source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The best bid was made by Dutch trader Vitol from among three bidders.</p>
<p>The tender closed on October 8 and offered 125,000 barrels of light naphtha for October 19-20 lifting. It is expected to be awarded by October 10.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703084)</p>
